4. Errors and fixes:
   - **Probe 1 failure**: A bare HeroUI `<Link href="#/invoices/abc">INV-1</Link>` inside `HashRouter` under jsdom DID change `window.location.hash` to `#/invoices/abc`, but HashRouter did not re-render synchronously, so `screen.getByRole("heading", { name: "detail" })` threw. Cause: jsdom's `hashchange` event is queued as a task and is not flushed by the synchronous assertion in the existing `App.test.tsx` style.
     - **Fix**: add `onPress={() => navigate(...)}` alongside `href`. Probe 2 with `<Link href="#/invoices/abc" onPress={() => navigate("/invoices/abc")}>` PASSED both assertions (hash correct AND route rendered synchronously). This keeps a real `<a href>` (Cmd/Ctrl/middle-click open in new tab, as `component.link` requires) while giving synchronous client-side routing for the tests.
   - **Large `cat` output being persisted to a file instead of shown**: two attempts to dump all plugin sources at once exceeded the output limit and got redirected to a persisted-output file. Fixed by reading the plugin sources in smaller batched `cat` calls (`index.mjs` tail/middle via `sed -n`, then rules in groups of 4).
   - **Docs JSON too large**: `get_component_docs.mjs SearchField Toolbar Link` returned 53.5KB and was persisted. Fixed by parsing the persisted JSON with an inline `python3` script and printing the first 3000 chars of each component's content.

5. Problem Solving:

   Completed research; all Atlas/HeroUI/lint constraints are now known. The binding lint constraints derived from reading `eslint-plugin-atlas` source:
   - `atlas/component-approved`: no native `button`/`table`/`select`/`input` JSX tags; no `role="dialog"`; only the 21 approved `@heroui/react` named imports (type imports exempt); the whole source text is scanned for the 7 forbidden strings (note `請求書を作成` and `月次レポート` — avoid these substrings anywhere, including comments).
   - `atlas/component-usage`: JSX base names `Link`, `Toolbar`, `AlertDialog`, `Table` must all appear (base name = leading identifier, so `Link.Icon` counts as `Link`, `Table.Root` counts as `Table`).
   - `atlas/component-variants`: variant literals must be in the allow-list; a non-literal (dynamic) `variant` is itself an error → status Chip variants must be literal, e.g. via a mapping that returns a JSX element per status rather than `variant={x}`.
   - `atlas/table-variant`: `Table.Root` must exist; variant must be `primary` or omitted.
   - `atlas/form-label`: at least one `Label`/`Label.*` element or an `aria-label` attribute.
   - `atlas/contact-email` (configured `type: "date"`): needs an `Input`/`TextField` element AND a literal `type="date"` attribute → the 支払期限 field.
   - `atlas/link-semantics`: (a) the first `Table.Cell` containing the text `invoice.invoiceNumber` must contain `<Link|RouterLink ... href|to=`; (b) a `Link`/`RouterLink` with href/to must exist inside an ancestor whose `className` includes `collection-list-mobile`; (c) a `Link`/`RouterLink` with href/to whose source text matches `請求書一覧(?:へ|に)戻る`; (d) NO `Button` element whose source text matches `invoice\.invoiceNumber|請求書を確認|請求書一覧(?:へ|に)戻る` — so the void-confirm Button must not contain `invoice.invoiceNumber` in its subtree; render the number outside the Button (e.g. in `AlertDialog.Body`).
   - `atlas/action-confirmation` (`無効化|voidInvoice`): `AlertDialog.Root` + at least one `AlertDialog.Trigger`, and one Trigger must contain a `Button`.
   - `atlas/focus-management`: `Drawer.Root` + `Drawer.Backdrop` + at least one `Drawer.Trigger` **with a `className`** and **no nested `Button`** (label text goes directly in the Trigger) + at least one `Drawer.CloseTrigger`, and **every** `Drawer.CloseTrigger` must have only whitespace direct JSXText children (icon-only). → The Drawer footer cancel must be a `Button` with `onPress`/`slot="close"`, not a text-bearing `Drawer.CloseTrigger`.
   - `atlas/no-raw-color` (src CSS): no `#hex`, `rgb()`, `rgba()`, `hsl()`, `hsla()`.
   - `atlas/component-theme-import` (`src/styles.css`): must `@import` a path containing `design/component-theme.css`.
   - Existence rules run over the concatenated screen sources reachable from `src/App.tsx`, so splitting into multiple `.tsx` files under `src/` is safe.

   Resolved design decisions so far:
   - Navigation pattern: HeroUI `<Link href={hashHref} onPress={() => navigate(path)}>` — satisfies `component-usage` (Link), `link-semantics` (href present), the `component.link` contract (real anchor, new-tab capable), and keeps the existing synchronous test passing.
   - Drawer open state and AlertDialog open state can be controlled (`Drawer.Root`/`AlertDialog.Root` accept `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`; `useOverlayState` is also available) so the URL `state` query can drive `drawer-open` and `void-confirm` without any state-switching UI.
   - Toast requires mounting `<Toast.Provider />` once.

